{"id":"u-adf225c3-c985-4947-846a-e613e990674a","src":"community","title":"Verkhoshansky Superposition Training","author":"Mithosphere","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/YLNxR0-superposition-training-yuri-verkhoshansky-1992","desc":"The core purpose of this program is to systematically shatter strength and muscular plateaus by leveraging the foundational Soviet sports science concept known as the Long-Term Delayed Training Effect (LTDE). Unlike standard western linear programming, which mistakenly assumes that fitness and fatigue must always climb at a steady rate, this program uses strategic, highly organized waves of extreme stress alternating with deep, active recovery to trigger explosive physical adaptations.\n\nHere is a breakdown of why this program exists and how it works:\n\n1. Exploiting the Superposition Principle\n\nIn a standard training split, you attempt to recover completely between workouts. Yuri Verkhoshansky discovered that for elite or heavily plateaued athletes, standard recovery is not a strong enough signal to force new muscle and strength gains. This program forces you to train past the point of recovery during High and Maximal weeks.\nYou are intentionally accumulating structural and neural fatigue across multiple weeks. By the end of a high block, your body is in a state of controlled overreaching. The true magic happens during the Low weeks: when you suddenly drop the volume, your body experiences a massive anabolic rebound. It builds back far past your previous baseline, a phenomenon known as supercompensation.\n\n2. Safeguarding the Central Nervous System (CNS)\n\nTrue absolute strength is driven by your brain's ability to recruit muscle fibers. If you lift near your maximum weight every week, your CNS fries, your technique breaks down, and your strength plummets.\nBy strictly separating your metrics—using Percentages Only for your main and supplemental compounds and RPE Only for accessories—the program keeps you precise where it counts, while allowing your body to auto-regulate secondary movements based on your daily fatigue levels. The mandatory SKIP ALL weeks are intentionally engineered into the spreadsheet to completely clear residual fatigue before it turns into chronic overtraining.\n\n3. Forcing Structural Muscle Hypertrophy\n\nBy locking in a strict group of compound movements (Squat, Bench, Deadlift, OHP) and their specific mechanical variations (Pause, Close-Grip, Deficit, Push Press) for 20 unbroken weeks, you remove the guesswork. Your body cannot rely on \"novelty\" to grow; it is forced to adapt structurally by thickening muscle fibers and reinforcing connective tissues to survive the wave-like surges in absolute workload.\n\nThe ultimate objective of this 20-microcycle, 4-mesocycle, single macrocycle is simple: You endure periods of calculated fatigue to unleash a delayed, compounding wave of absolute power, culminating in personal records by Week 20.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-15T22:50:41.368Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Lower A: Moderate","Upper A: Moderate","Lower B: Moderate","Upper B: Moderate"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":75,"x":4}]},{"n":"Squat (Paused)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":70,"x":4}]},{"n":"Box Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":70,"x":4}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":75,"x":4}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Close Grip)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":70,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":70,"x":4}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe"